Builds on the QuestTalkFixture PR (test fixture only).

Problem. Romeo & Juliet had no quest script: Romeo, Juliet, Father
Lawrence, the Apothecary, Draul Leptoc and Phillipa had no quest
dialogue, the cadava potion could not be made, and varp 144 (rjquest),
which the client and Quest Helper read, was never set. The Apothecary's
potion-making interface (556) had no handler either.

Change.
- Progress is varp 144 with the OSRS stages: 0, 10 find Juliet, 20 take
  her message, 30 see Father Lawrence, 40 see the Apothecary, 50 bring
  cadava berries / the potion to Juliet, 60 tell Romeo, 100 complete
  (checked against the cache dbrow at startup). Reward: 5 QP.
- Quest dialogue follows the wiki transcript for every stage, including
  Romeo's six random openers, lost / duplicate messages ("Why are you
  waving that around at me..." when the message is used on Romeo), the
  berry questions, and the option menus that come back after each answer.
- Juliet drinking the potion: after the hand-over the cutscene's lines play
  as dialogue (Juliet, Phillipa, Draul Leptoc, the player); the crypt
  scene's lines play when Romeo is told, then the quest completes.
- Side dialogue: Draul Leptoc's four-option menu before the message, the
  "Sir Draul notices the message!" and "Draul notices the potion!"
  branches, his full stage 40/50 lines; Phillipa's full lines at every
  stage; Juliet's "Romeo, Romeo, wherefore art thou Romeo?" before the
  quest and her four lines after it; Romeo's after-quest lines; Father
  Lawrence's not-started menu (quest / kill / bar / ok, each returning to
  the menu) and his whiskey lines plus one of two random lines after the
  potion.
- Apothecary: "Can you make potions for me?" (and his Potions op) opens
  Apothecary's Potions (interface 556): strength potion (limpwurt root,
  red spiders' eggs, 5 coins), energy potion (2 limpwurt roots, chocolate
  dust) and antipoison (limpwurt root, cadava berries, 5 coins), each
  Buy-1/5/X/All, making as many as every ingredient and the coins allow,
  in one inventory transaction. "Talk about something else." has the
  gossip option (not started / completed answers), the hair and charity
  answers return to his menu with their trailing lines, the free sample
  gives a spot cream (acne potion) about half the time, only if the player
  has none. Cadava berries used on him after the quest: "I don't need
  those any more."
- Cadava potion: Look-at shows the warning box; Drink outside the
  Apothecary's shop refuses, inside it asks to confirm, then the
  black-out lines and the Apothecary's "Blimey... you've been out for
  hours!".

Tests. RomeoAndJulietInteractionTest (14): the full quest on varp 144
(0 -> 100, items handed over and taken, cutscene lines, after-quest Romeo
and Juliet), random opener and quoted correction, Romeo's returning menu,
lost message and the hidden quest topic, berries on the first visit, the
potions option opening interface 556, gossip / hair returning to the menu,
the free sample (one at a time, charity line), berries after the quest,
Father Lawrence before / after, Draul's menu and both carried-item
branches, Phillipa's lines, a spare message on Romeo, Look-at / Drink of
the potion inside and outside the shop. ApothecaryPotionsTest (6): Potions
op opens 556, strength stops at the scarcest ingredient, antipoison stops
when the coins run out, energy takes two roots and no coins, nothing is
taken without every ingredient, a full inventory still brews.

Data sources. OSRS Wiki: Romeo & Juliet, Transcript:Romeo & Juliet,
Transcript:Romeo, Transcript:Juliet, Transcript:Father Lawrence,
Transcript:Apothecary, Apothecary (Talk-to / Potions ops, products,
free sample ~1/2, Changes), Apothecary's Potions (stock and ingredients,
the 18 October 2018 coin change), Potion (Apothecary); Quest Helper
RomeoAndJuliet (varp 144 steps 0-60); interface apothecary_potions.if3
(osrs-dumps: Buy-1/5/X/All ops, title/contents/pic components); cache: npc
5036 ops, obj 756 ops (Look-at, Drink); the spot cream lines ("Ok then. Try
this potion." / "Only that spot cream. Hope you enjoy it.") from the
LostCity 2004 apothecary script.

Caveats.
- The two cutscenes are dialogue only: no camera pans, NPC movement,
  Juliet's drinking animation, the crypt scene or the two jingles ("Cadava
  Potion", "Romeo Falls in Love"); their staging is not documented in
  enough detail. Romeo does not walk up to nearby players.
- Apothecary's Potions: the row title / contents texts, the made and
  missing-ingredient messages, and keeping the interface open after a
  purchase are guesses (no transcript of the interface).
- Gossip during the quest uses the not-started answer (undocumented).
- Father Lawrence at stages 10/20 uses his not-started menu; Juliet at
  stage 60 and Phillipa after the quest are undocumented (box / default).
- Drinking the cadava potion at the shop uses it up and does not change
  hitpoints or shake the screen; the shop bounds are the Apothecary's
  wander square (3195, 3404, radius 3).
- The Combat path voucher, A Tail of Two Cats and Ratcatchers options of
  the Apothecary are not part of this PR.
- The journal texts (reworked in OSRS on 14 January 2026) and chathead
  expressions are best guesses.

